# writing.zd — the `static` placement, running.
#
# The milestone-7 target is a `client` + `static` application (§14C.3b):
# content fixed at build time, plus whatever the reader is doing right
# now. This file is the smallest program that is one.
#
# `posts` is `static`, so it is computed once by `zdc build`, on the build
# host, and **inlined into the bundle as a literal**. Read from the view it
# is `List of Post` and not `Remote of List of Post`, because no boundary
# is crossed — §5.2's Rule 1 is satisfied here rather than excepted
# (§14G.1.4).
#
# The consequences are visible in `dist/`: `client.js` contains the titles
# as JavaScript literals, emits no `$remote` binding for them, and `dist/`
# has no `functions/` directory at all. There is no request to make.

record Post
    slug  is Text
    title is Text
    year  is Whole

state posts is static List of Post starting [(Post with slug is "hello-world", title is "Hello, world", year is 2024), (Post with slug is "on-placement", title is "Placement is a property of state", year is 2025), (Post with slug is "no-network", title is "The network is in the type", year is 2026)]

# Derived at build time from build-time data: still `static`, still free.
# The whole derivation runs on the build host and only its result ships.
state heading is static Text from titleFor with posts

function titleFor with all
    give "Writing"

# What the reader is doing. `client`, because it is theirs and it is gone
# on reload — which is correct.
state query is client Text starting ""

view
    Column
        Heading heading
        Input query, hint is "filter posts"

        each post in posts
            Row
                Text post.title
                Text post.slug
